==English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|frm|en}} {{m|frm|palliatif}}, from {{etyl|NL.|en}} *palliativus, from {{etyl|ML.|en}} {{m|la|palliare||to cloak}}, from {{etyl|la|en}} {{m|la|pallium||a cloak}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|/ˈpalɪətɪv/|lang=en}}
* {{a|GenAm}} {{IPA|/ˈpælieɪtɪv/|/ˈpæliətɪv/|lang=en}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj}}

# Serving to palliate; serving to extenuate or mitigate.
# {{lb|en|medicine}} Minimising the progression of a [[disease]] and relieving [[undesirable]] [[symptoms]] for as long as possible, rather than attempting to cure the (usually [[incurable]]) disease.

====Synonyms====
* {{sense|medicine}}

====Coordinate terms====
* {{sense|medicine}} {{l|en|analgesic}}, {{l|en|lenitive}}

====Related terms====
* {{l|en|palliate}}
* {{l|en|palliation}}

